{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted","id":1126616,"title":"Custom character creation xp-scale [opinion wanted!]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T01:10:54-07:00","id":1126616,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Custom character creation xp-scale [opinion wanted!]","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready to start my next VtR 2E chronicle. I ran a test game during this summer. Based on the experiences from that game and reading the example characters given in the books I have created a custom XP-scale for my next game. I would like some constructive criticism. This feels about right to me, but I haven't run a lot of VtR 2E games.<br /> <br /> Neonate: 10-15 xp<br /> Ancilla: 25-35 xp<br /> Elder: 80-100 xp<br /> <br /> Link to a mock up of an Elder created with this XP-scale --&gt; <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-UNjCh1t9ogd1BzU2NfMklxWkU\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-...1BzU2NfMklxWkU</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:07:09-07:00","id":1126622,"title":"","content":"What's the rationale for using this instead of the official one on page 82 of VtR 2e? It's kind of hard to give much criticism without the reasoning for the change. Your rules seem to inflate the lower ends significantly. I mean, there's a gap of 45 XP between a high end Ancilla, and a low end Elder.. even though a powerful ancilla and a weak elder are supposed to be pretty close to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:46:29-07:00","id":1126633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126622#post1126622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the rationale for using this instead of the official one on page 82 of VtR 2e? It's kind of hard to give much criticism without the reasoning for the change. Your rules seem to inflate the lower ends significantly. I mean, there's a gap of 45 XP between a high end Ancilla, and a low end Elder.. even though a powerful ancilla and a weak elder are supposed to be pretty close to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, torpor is a great equalizer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T02:57:11-07:00","id":1126636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126622#post1126622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the rationale for using this instead of the official one on page 82 of VtR 2e? It's kind of hard to give much criticism without the reasoning for the change. Your rules seem to inflate the lower ends significantly. I mean, there's a gap of 45 XP between a high end Ancilla, and a low end Elder.. even though a powerful ancilla and a weak elder are supposed to be pretty close to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see Ancillae and Elders as equals in any way.<br /> <br /> The rational is that it feels wrong. I feel like Elders are supposed to be the exception to the rule. The cockroaches that somehow managed to survive centuries despite every probability of getting hunted down, backstabbed or Diablerized along the way. The handful that actually made it. There's a significant gap between Ancillae and Elders, because that's how the example antagonists are written in the books. You just look at the examples in chapter five of the core rulebook or chapter five in Thousand Years of Night. That's where all the bad ass monsters are, but I can't get even close with 35xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:00:55-07:00","id":1126637,"title":"","content":"To me the Kindred are the monsters. I don't need special rules or exceptions to make monsters, because they are already in the covenants and clans. I'm just looking for a way to scale things in a way that feels approximately right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T03:54:46-07:00","id":1126643,"title":"","content":"While I agree with your sentiment that active elders should have a gap in xp disparity between them and a neonate. Your elder is just a murder hobo with 5 Humanity. I'm not buying a character who spends his time firebombing others, fomenting violence and fighting tooth and claw has a Humanity rating that high. He hasn't gotten a single one of his clan's signatory disciplines to 5, he hasn't gotten any skills, except brawl past 3. He's a Carthian who doesn't have a single ally or contact.<br /> <br /> But this is an excellent example of my problem with the character build rules. I can see similar designs with starting Mekhet and Daeva, toss them 5-10 xp and it's ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:11:39-07:00","id":1126662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126643#post1126643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your elder is just a murder hobo with 5 Humanity. I'm not buying a character who spends his time firebombing others, fomenting violence and fighting tooth and claw has a Humanity rating that high.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably should drop this monster to Humanity 3 or 4, but I feel like that's irrelevant to this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126643#post1126643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He hasn't gotten a single one of his clan's signatory disciplines to 5, he hasn't gotten any skills, except brawl past 3. He's a Carthian who doesn't have a single ally or contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to build cities where there's only one or two NPCs (per' clan) who actually get a signature Discipline to 5. All the Neonates are stuck at 1-2 dots, while Ancillae and Elders are rocking 3rd and 4th level powers with the ultimate bad asses getting access to the 5th level powers. It's a simple way to build power fantasy for the players. Also, having three dots in a skill is supposed to be enough for a successful professional career. Having four dots is supposed to be rare, while anyone with five dots in a skill is supposed to be downright legendary. That's what the books say, anyhow, so it's how I build the NPCs. Player characters are a different matter altogether, of course.<br /> <br /> That way when the player characters get to a fifth dot in anything it means something. They can do things that only a handful of others in the entire city can do. Sadly, the Thousand Years of Night didn't come with detailed descriptions of Disciplines past the 5th dot, unlike Guide to the Camarilla or Guide to the Sabbat (it's been a while, so I don't quite remember). I know, poor example, but the only ones that I can think of when it comes to details of higher level Disciplines. Instead I give powerful characters a wider selection of Disciplines and a few Devotions to go along with those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126643#post1126643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is an excellent example of my problem with the character build rules. I can see similar designs with starting Mekhet and Daeva, toss them 5-10 xp and it's ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, I dropped around 80xp on that monster, but still felt like I could have spent another 10-15 on a lot of small details.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:47:54-07:00","id":1126681,"title":"","content":"I bump Neonates and Ancillae up 0-11, and Elders 11-20 from the recommended starting values depending on their completion of Climbing the Ladder and Spinning the Web. Works pretty well for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:40:30-07:00","id":1126741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126636#post1126636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Ancillae and Elders as equals in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what I'm getting at is, do you feel the game wants this to be the case and doesn't live up to it, or are you trying to house rule the game to be more like this?<br /> <br /> Because the game as written isn't like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ancilla (an \u2022 SILL \u2022 uh): Kindred too old to be considered neonates, but not yet elders, whose Requiem has lasted roughly 50 to 150 years. The plural is ancillae (an \u2022 SILL \u2022 ae).&quot;<br /> &quot;elder: A vampire who has survived for over 150 years; also a term of respect.&quot;<br /> <br /> VtR 2e presents a relatively smooth transition from neonate, to ancilla, to elder. Your average ancilla might be no much for your average elder, but the two groups are supposed to &quot;touch&quot; at the extremes.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm trying to get some clarity here. If you just don't want this, that's a very different thing than if you feel the chart in the books doesn't reflect what the books say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like Elders are supposed to be the exception to the rule. </div> </div> </div>Where does it say this? Why is there a whole supplement dedicated to elder level play if they're supposed to be such outliers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a significant gap between Ancillae and Elders, because that's how the example antagonists are written in the books. You just look at the examples in chapter five of the core rulebook or chapter five in Thousand Years of Night. That's where all the bad ass monsters are, but I can't get even close with 35xp. </div> </div> </div>The bonus XP are their for building PCs, not NPCs. Inflating where the PCs start only inflates were antagonists have to be to give the PCs dramatic tension. Upping the ante has appeals, but it shouldn't go to the NPCs, because the NPCs aren't going to grow like the PCs are.<br /> <br /> As well, if you're planning an elders game and want to boost things, using the Thousand Years of Night creation rules (and Spinning the Web as per Charlaquin's post) with a base of 25 XP on top of all that, creates some pretty heavy hitters. Are they one on one matches for some of the book's NPCs? No. But those NPCs are meant to be potential solo (not counting underlings) antagonists to a coterie characters created with those rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:56:49-07:00","id":1126750,"title":"","content":"You only need one century to qualify as an Elder by RAW. Even if you change that, you're an Ancilla until you are an Elder, so unless there is some special super-powerup that happens when one becomes an Elder, it should be more of a gradient. Probably with overlap, since an active Ancilla could have more XP than an Elder that survived so long by keeping their head down and not exercising their abilities much.<br /> <br /> Maybe the fiction Elders are more potent, but you bear the Elder title from 100 years to 1000 years, whereupon you become an Ancient. They should probably have a huge range of power to account for that. A new Elder shouldn't really be much stronger than an old Ancilla, once again barring some mystical powerup.<br /> <br /> I feel like people get hung up with what are, essentially, in-game titles that indicate respect for vampires that survive a certain amount of time. It doesn't indicate some fundamental change in what that vampire is.<br /> <br /> And I feel like once you start getting to where older vampires are just flat-out better because of mystical reasons rather than intelligence and ability, you start going back to Masquerade design principles rather than Requiem. Maybe that's what you want, I don't know. You still seem kind of vague on why you think this is necessary and what your design goals are for making the change. Nobody can really help you if your only explanation is &quot;the current method feels wrong.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 08-09-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:06:46-07:00","id":1126754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126662#post1126662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That way when the player characters get to a fifth dot in anything it means something. They can do things that only a handful of others in the entire city can do. Sadly, the Thousand Years of Night didn't come with detailed descriptions of Disciplines past the 5th dot, unlike Guide to the Camarilla or Guide to the Sabbat (it's been a while, so I don't quite remember). I know, poor example, but the only ones that I can think of when it comes to details of higher level Disciplines. Instead I give powerful characters a wider selection of Disciplines and a few Devotions to go along with those.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason there are no writeups of Disciplines past the 5th dot is that Disciplines only go as far as the 5th dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:22:25-07:00","id":1126760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126643#post1126643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with your sentiment that active elders should have a gap in xp disparity between them and a neonate. Your elder is just a murder hobo with 5 Humanity. I'm not buying a character who spends his time firebombing others, fomenting violence and fighting tooth and claw has a Humanity rating that high. She hasn't gotten a single one of his clan's signatory disciplines to 5, she hasn't gotten any skills, except brawl past 3. She's a Carthian who doesn't have a single ally or contact.<br /> <br /> But this is an excellent example of my problem with the character build rules. I can see similar designs with starting Mekhet and Daeva, toss them 5-10 xp and it's ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wish I could like this post twice, thank you for posting it. I agree with your critical deconstruction and social commentary about the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RPGsEqualCombat\" target=\"_blank\">RPG equal Combat</a> mindset and the unlikeliness of a <a href=\"http://www.urbandictionary.com/define.php?term=murderhobo\" target=\"_blank\">Murder Hobo</a> surviving more than a couple decades, let alone centuries.<br /> <br /> I also agree about the sentiment that active elders should have a gap in xp disparity between them and a neonate. Not having to lay low in a way Torpor allows while living centuries is a sign of great success in cultivating a support network.<br /> <br /> Elders that didn't get Torpored are much more likely to have a web of support ensuring feeding and that they would never even have to face combat in the first place rather than being extremely talented at combat.<br /> <br /> [rhetorical] <i>Who's more likely to survive and prosper, a friendless homeless refugee scrapping by without a steady job or a CEO in a gated mansion with security guards, food delivered to the door and prepared by a house chef, and friends that also have those types of assets that'll go to bat for them? </i>[/rhetorical] Same principles in vampire society unless you are running an urban fantasy where real-life societal-logic-need-not apply. I think understanding a hypothetical vampire society is about understanding their weaknesses and vulnerability, more than their powers and strengths and vampires must withstand several hour stretches of complete helplessness every 24 hours without a support system no matter how awesome they may be in combat.<br /> <br /> The hypothetical Elder doesn't even have a Safe Place to rest their head in the day and seems like she'd be the first to &quot;disappear&quot; if the leaders of the Domain are not also Carthians because of how easily found she'd be and how much trouble she obviously is waiting to happen. Heck, a single Player Character with <u>NO XP</u> could easily have that Elder staked, killed, Diablerized, or worse unless the storyteller was extending the benefits of mechanics to the Elder not on the sheet or otherwise protected via some <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PlotImmunity\" target=\"_blank\">Plot Immunity</a>. Character's like that get embraced and maybe cause a disruption or two and then disappear before a decade into their Requiems in the setting as presented in Canon. The <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/PlotImmunity\" target=\"_blank\">Plot Immunity</a> that'd be needed for that character to reach that age of Elder is staggering.<br /> <br /> Back on topic,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126681#post1126681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bump Neonates and Ancillae up 0-11, and Elders 11-20 from the recommended starting values depending on their completion of Climbing the Ladder and Spinning the Web. Works pretty well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems extremely reasonable and incentives to use those steps to flesh-out PCs and NPCs alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-09-2017, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:42:24-07:00","id":1126786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126741#post1126741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess what I'm getting at is, do you feel the game wants this to be the case and doesn't live up to it, or are you trying to house rule the game to be more like this?<br /> <br /> Because the game as written isn't like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ancilla (an \u2022 SILL \u2022 uh): Kindred too old to be considered neonates, but not yet elders, whose Requiem has lasted roughly 50 to 150 years. The plural is ancillae (an \u2022 SILL \u2022 ae).&quot;<br /> &quot;elder: A vampire who has survived for over 150 years; also a term of respect.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better, if the line for Elders is drawn at 250 years, but that's a purely arbitary line that I'm drawing, because I feel like it. I'm actually starting to notice that most of the &quot;issues&quot; that I'm experiencing are from two things. I have expectations that come from Vampire: the Masquerade, where Elders were these god-like beings that were more like forces of nature than actual vampires. And then I'm getting signals from players who want the same thing. They want the Elders to be ancient, monstrous and significantly more powerful. I find it undesirable to have a city full of these monsters, so the logical step is to have only a few Elders. Most of them just don't make it or decide that a permanent change of scenery is preferable to Final Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126741#post1126741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I'm trying to get some clarity here. If you just don't want this, that's a very different thing than if you feel the chart in the books doesn't reflect what the books say.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main concern is what the players say. If enough players come to me and say that they feel that the Elders don't feel like Elders, then they are not Elders. I then house rule things until they feel like Elders. RAW is only there to provide a common starting point for a game. During every game of any significant length that I have run the rules have been fudged and changed to accommodate the players, while at the same time providing an illusion of fairness. It's only an illusion, though, so I kindly ask all the players not to intentionally break the game. It happens regardless, but then we just deal with it like adults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126741#post1126741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does it say this? Why is there a whole supplement dedicated to elder level play if they're supposed to be such outliers?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hold over from a decade of playing Vampire: the Masquerade. I like the idea, so regardless of what the books say that's how I run things. To me Thousand Years of Night felt like a book about Ancillae rather than Elders, but that's just me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126741#post1126741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bonus XP are their for building PCs, not NPCs. Inflating where the PCs start only inflates were antagonists have to be to give the PCs dramatic tension. Upping the ante has appeals, but it shouldn't go to the NPCs, because the NPCs aren't going to grow like the PCs are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the PCs feel weak, then the players are not going to get their power fantasy. At the end of the day this is entertainment, and I don't have a problem with playing into players' power fantasies while still telling captivating stories. If that requires that I up the XP across the board then I don't really see that as a big problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T12:06:29-07:00","id":1126799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126750#post1126750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I feel like once you start getting to where older vampires are just flat-out better because of mystical reasons rather than intelligence and ability, you start going back to Masquerade design principles rather than Requiem. Maybe that's what you want, I don't know. You still seem kind of vague on why you think this is necessary and what your design goals are for making the change. Nobody can really help you if your only explanation is &quot;the current method feels wrong.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Before I read your comment I couldn't really put my finger on why Vampire: the Requiem 2E felt &quot;wrong&quot; to me. Then I read your comment and it clicked. Without this discussions I might still be frustrated, because I did not understand why I'm feeling dissatisfied with how the game is written. Going forward, I'll be able to provide a clear disclaimer to all players who want to join my games.<br /> <br /> I could simply go play Vampire: the Masquerade, but I haven't felt like doing that since 2004 or so. nWoD had a very clear design philosophy of throwing tons of tools at me and then letting me do whatever I wanted with those tools. I loved that design philosophy, even if some of the tools were clunky and didn't really fit together as well as advertised. With the 2E books the plenthora of subsystems have been streamlined and cleaned up a lot, but I also feel like the variety in the toolbox has lessened. Reading the books I get more of a &quot;this is how this thing is supposed to work&quot; -kind of feel. And I don't always agree with what the books are trying to tell me. That's why I feel like house ruling the system to suit my personal tastes.<br /> <br /> Going forward I can clearly communicate to everyone that the Vampire: the Requiem 2E games I run will have more of a Vampire: the Masquerade Revised <b>feel</b> when it comes to power level. Without actually having any VtM content or game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T12:06:49-07:00","id":1126801,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> You don't want elders; you want ancients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T12:23:16-07:00","id":1126805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1126616-custom-character-creation-xp-scale-opinion-wanted?p=1126801#post1126801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2648_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2648\" data-vbnamecard=\"2648\">TelperionST</a> You don't want elders; you want ancients.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like we are arguing semantics here, but yes, I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:44:48-07:00","id":1126936,"title":"","content":"I mean, it is semantics, but it's important semantics because what VtR calls things isn't the same as what VtM called things.<br /> <br /> In VtR &quot;ancient&quot; is the term for what you're calling elder: the vampires with immense and legendary power that count centuries like others count decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}